president Trump getting aggressive with  his foreign policy tonight he's closing  the Palestine Liberation office here in  Washington as punishment for the group's  rejection of peace talks with Israel  he's also firing a shot across the bow  of the International Criminal Court the  ICC the announcements were made by the  president's national security advisor  this afternoon correspondent Jillian  Turner has specifics today on the eve of  September the 11th I want to deliver a  clear and unambiguous message on behalf  of the President of the United States  the Trump administration's got the ICC  in its crosshairs today the United  States will use any means necessary to  protect our citizens and those of our  allies from unjust prosecution by this  illegitimate court and Bolling's not  taking any prisoners  we will not cooperate with the ICC we  will let the ICC die on its own after  all for all intents and purposes the ICC  is already dead to us and he didn't stop  there showing the US isn't afraid to  flex more than one foreign policy muscle  at a time next up on Bolton's hit list  the Palestinian Liberation Organization  or PLO the Department of State will  announce the closure of the Palestine  Liberation Organization office here in  Washington DC the State Department  explained the decision a few hours ago  saying the PLO has quote condemned a  u.s. peace plan they have not yet seen  and refused to engage with the US  government with respect to peace efforts  fully making clear when it comes to the  israeli-palestinian conflict the Trump  administration is officially taking  sides the United States will always  stand with our friend and ally Israel  but the Palestinians are punching back  calling on the ICC to immediately open  an investigation into Israel saying  quote we reiterate that the rights of  the Palestinian people are not for sale  that we will not succumb to us threats  and bullying and that we will continue  our legitimate struggle for freedom  Bolton also had words of warning for the  ICC when it comes to the war in  Afghanistan threatening US sanctions  against ICC judges should they launch an  investigation into what they say may  war crimes committed by the American  military and Intel community in  Afghanistan though the US has never been  a member of the ICC and has always kept  the court at arm's length this would be  the first time in history America  imposed sanctions on court judges the  ICC prosecutor has requested to  investigate these Americans for alleged  detainee abuse an utterly unfounded  unjustifiable investigation Bolton's  going all in to protect American  soldiers who've served in the 17 year  long war in Afghanistan he also invoked  president Trump's first major foreign  affairs speech back in 2016 in which he  promised to put American the American  people's security above all else Bolton  said today the administration's renewing  its commitment to an America first  foreign policy Brett Jillian thank you
 

